name: the kit
boss: quartermaster
flavor: The rest of what you carry -- reach for the right one without looking.
brief: The arsenal is not only weapons. A text browser, a PDF reader, offline
brief: Wikipedia, a name-finder, a language to glue it all together, even a
brief: game for the long nights. This level is knowing which tool is which and
brief: how you reach for it -- most are things you run and use, not drills, so
brief: (``example.com`` is a name set aside for teaching -- it belongs to
brief: nobody, so looking up its sub-addresses bothers no real site.)
brief: here you name the invocation. As always, any target is ``127.0.0.1`` or
brief: something you own.
tools: links subfinder dnsx mutool kiwix-serve kiwix-search frotz python
lab: web
---
q: @weburl@ -- {read it as plain text in the terminal, with|get it down to plain text without opening a browser, using|skip the browser and turn it into text you can read in the shell, with} `links`
a: links -dump @weburl@
out: practice site
ref: links
teach: links
hint: -dump prints the page's text and exits, no interactive browser
---
q: {print the sum of 2 and 2|add 2 and 2 and print the result|work out what 2 plus 2 comes out to}, with `python`
a: python3 -c "print(2 + 2)"
a: python -c "print(2 + 2)"
out: ^4$
ref: python
teach: python
hint: python3 -c runs a one-line program; print() shows the result
---
q: {find a company's hidden sub-addresses for|enumerate every subdomain hanging off|dig up the sub-addresses tucked under} ``example.com``, with `subfinder`, quietly
a: subfinder -d example.com -silent
ref: subfinder
teach: subfinder
hint: -d the domain, -silent for just the names
---
q: {resolve the names in|turn every name listed in|look up addresses for each name in} ``names.txt`` to addresses, with `dnsx`, showing the response
a: dnsx -l names.txt -a -resp
ref: dnsx
teach: dnsx
hint: -l the list, -a for A records, -resp to show the answer
---
q: {pull the words out of|strip the text out of|get everything readable out of} ``file.pdf`` as plain text, with `mutool`
a: mutool draw -F txt file.pdf
ref: mutool
teach: mutool
hint: draw -F txt renders the pdf to text
---
q: {serve the offline archives on port|get the local knowledge dump reachable on port|open up the offline wiki collection on port} ``8080``, with `kiwix-serve`
a: kiwix-serve --port 8080 archive.zim
ref: kiwix-serve
teach: kiwix-serve
hint: --port then the .zim file to serve
---
q: ``wiki.zim`` -- {search it for|see if it mentions|check it for a hit on} ``first aid``, with `kiwix-search`
a: kiwix-search wiki.zim 'first aid'
ref: kiwix-search
teach: kiwix-search
hint: the .zim file, then the phrase in quotes
---
q: ``story.z5`` -- {play the text adventure|fire up the story and start playing|dive into the adventure}, with `frotz`
a: frotz story.z5
ref: frotz
teach: frotz
hint: frotz takes the story file; then you type where to go
